# Orion-X Phoenix Edition — quit the Plymouth splash before the first-boot
# wizard takes tty1.
#
# @decision DEC-PHASE13-030
# @canonical
# @category BOOT
# @date 2026-11-01
# @title Plymouth is quit from a unit with no TTY, never from the wizard's own
#   exec context (#141)
# @status accepted
# @rationale The QEMU boot flake (#141, one firmware mode per run, BIOS and
#   UEFI both seen) is a deadlock in systemd's pre-exec TTY setup, not a wedged
#   plymouthd. orionx-first-boot.service is StandardInput=tty on /dev/tty1
#   with TTYReset=yes, so BEFORE it can exec anything — including its old
#   `ExecStartPre=plymouth quit` — systemd's child acquires tty1, takes the
#   /dev/console lock and resets the terminal (exec-invoke.c, v257). plymouthd
#   still owns tty1 at that moment because the only thing that would quit it is
#   that very ExecStartPre; some of the time the reset blocks on tty1, the child
#   never execs (`ps` shows it as "(timeout)", the pre-exec name), it holds the
#   console lock forever, serial-getty@ttyS0's child then blocks on the same
#   lock (wchan locks_lock_inode_wait), and no login prompt ever prints. The
#   run 41272254094 diagnostics block (ORIONX-PLYMOUTH-DIAG) shows exactly
#   that: plymouthd healthy in epoll_wait, "(timeout)" holding fds 0-2 on tty1
#   and fd 3 on /dev/console, "(agetty)" waiting on the lock.
#   The stock answer already exists: getty@.service is After=plymouth-quit-wait
#   so it never touches a VT while plymouth owns it, and plymouth-quit.service
#   quits the splash from a unit with no TTY. On this image lightdm.service
#   Conflicts= and replaces plymouth-quit.service (it quits plymouth itself),
#   so on first boot nothing quits the splash before the wizard — hence the
#   ExecStartPre hack (DEC-PHASE11-044) and the deadlock. This unit is the
#   first-boot stand-in for plymouth-quit.service: no TTY, no console lock,
#   nothing to block on; the wizard Wants= it and orders After= it and after
#   plymouth-quit-wait.service, so by the time systemd prepares tty1 for the
#   wizard, plymouthd is gone. It runs only while the wizard's own guard file
#   is absent; later boots leave the splash to lightdm as before.
# @see orionx-first-boot.service, DEC-PHASE11-044, DEC-PHASE13-028
#
#   Decision Log entry as hand-written on 2026-11-01 (merged into this block
#   by #97, which made the block the authority): Plymouth is quit from a unit
#   with no TTY, never from the first-boot wizard's own exec context: new
#   `orionx-plymouth-quit.service` (`ExecStart=-/usr/bin/plymouth quit`,
#   `TimeoutStartSec=20`, the wizard's first-boot guard, no TTY settings), and
#   `orionx-first-boot.service` `Wants=` it and orders `After=` it and
#   `plymouth-quit-wait.service`, the rule the stock `getty@.service` follows;
#   the wizard's `ExecStartPre=plymouth quit` is gone. Supersedes the
#   ExecStartPre part of DEC-PHASE11-044 and the `timeout 10` part of
#   DEC-PHASE13-028. Root cause of the QEMU boot flake (#141), from the first
#   two `ORIONX-PLYMOUTH-DIAG` blocks (runs 41272254094 and 41272250733, both
#   BIOS, identical signature): plymouthd alive and not blocked (`epoll_wait`
#   in one, on CPU in the other); the wizard's pre-exec child (`(timeout)`,
#   never execed) holding tty1 on fds 0-2 and the `/dev/console` lock on fd 3;
#   serial-getty's `(agetty)` child in `locks_lock_inode_wait` on that lock;
#   no login prompt. systemd v257 `exec-invoke.c` acquires, locks and resets a
#   `StandardInput=tty`/`TTYReset=yes` unit's TTY before exec, and the wizard
#   did that to tty1 while plymouthd owned the VT because the only thing that
#   would quit the splash was the command waiting to exec; `lightdm.service`
#   `Conflicts=` the stock `plymouth-quit.service`, so nothing else quits it
#   on first boot. A `timeout` around a command cannot bound a block that
#   happens before exec. The diag script now records stack/wchan/syscall of
#   every console holder and pre-exec child plus `/proc/locks`. Evidence of
#   the fix: the PR's own QEMU runs; not reproduced locally

[Unit]
Description=Orion-X: quit the Plymouth splash before the first-boot wizard takes tty1
After=plymouth-start.service systemd-user-sessions.service
ConditionPathExists=!/var/lib/orionx/.first-boot-done

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=yes
# `-`: non-fatal when plymouthd is not running (splash disabled, or already
# gone). No StandardInput=tty / TTYPath here, deliberately: that is the whole
# point of this unit.
ExecStart=-/usr/bin/plymouth quit
# `plymouth quit` returns when plymouthd acknowledges; a splash that does not
# answer must not hold onboarding. Same bound as the stock plymouth-quit.service.
TimeoutStartSec=20
